    "body": "Escalated from effort:medium to effort:high. The case needs toolpath behavior that the current generator refuses.\n\nAt upstream/main 58cb641ca, Rotary Contour refuses a workpiece along X.\nSee `rotary_contour` in `crates/motion/src/multiaxis/rotary.rs:76`.\nIts height conversion divides by the axis Z component. Removing the refusal alone cannot support an A-axis workpiece.\nIssue #3000 tracks this refusal. I linked it on #2392. Related height work is in #2774.\n\nThe new pin `wrapped_case_keeps_three_rotary_operations_and_posts_a_axis_moves` compiled and failed on unchanged code.\nIt failed because `wrapped.camproj` is absent.\nThe existing test `the_kinds_refuse_each_other_degenerate_stances_by_name` passed. It requires the X-axis Contour refusal.\n\nHeld work: `mkinney:issue/2869-wrapped-a-axis`, commit cab66a8e28a9f0b2f5791c29da8028db0f9f9aea.\nThis branch contains only the failing catalog pin. There is no PR.\nSelf-review: the single new-file hunk requires the three saved rotary kinds and finite, varying A words in each posted section.\nIt prevents a catalog case that omits an operation or posts no rotary movement.\n\nI kept the named refusal. I did not omit Contour or weaken its guard.\nGenerator and safety changes need a worker at the safety floor.\nNo implementation, catalog assets, or goldens changed. The quick gate, clippy, and mutation checks did not run.\n\nThe inherited sccache wrapper stalled. Unsetting RUSTC_WRAPPER allowed both foreground test commands to finish.\nThe sandbox refused the read-only ps command. No approval prompt occurred.\nClaim released. The case is blocked by #3000.\n",
